## Appendix: Duplicate Review

I checked local vLLM submission bundles, private-visible vLLM advisories, and GitHub PR/issue search for `top_logprobs`, `prompt_logprobs`, `max_logprobs`, `top_n`, `CandidateTokens`, and gRPC logprob variants.

Nearby but distinct:

- `this report` / `GHSA-6pgw-f3pv-4h8q`: explicit candidate token IDs bypass `logprob_token_ids` bounds. This report covers count-based top-k selection and unsigned-to-signed overflow.
- `this report` / `GHSA-w2v2-5662-8v5q`: prompt token-ID range validation.
- `GHSA-3mwp-wvh9-7528`: unbounded OpenAI `n` fan-out DoS. This report uses a different gRPC response selector and a different lower sampler sink.

Public PR `#44680` names `top_logprobs`/`prompt_logprobs` as out-of-scope vectors that need `max_logprobs` wiring. PR `#45390` does not touch Rust gRPC files. Public GitHub PR and issue searches for the exact Rust gRPC `CandidateTokens.top_n` path returned no matches.
